Kernel 7.3 removed the task_euid() macro from linux/cred.h (task_uid()
remains). The vendored Rust helper still calls it, breaking bindings
generation and the helper compile:

  error: call to undeclared function 'task_euid'

task_euid() expanded to task_cred_xxx(task, euid); use that directly.

diff --git a/fs/vendor/kernel-rust/helpers/task.c b/fs/vendor/kernel-rust/helpers/task.c
--- a/fs/vendor/kernel-rust/helpers/task.c
+++ b/fs/vendor/kernel-rust/helpers/task.c
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ __rust_helper kuid_t rust_helper_task_uid(struct task_struct *task)
 
 __rust_helper kuid_t rust_helper_task_euid(struct task_struct *task)
 {
-	return task_euid(task);
+	return task_cred_xxx(task, euid);
 }
 
 #ifndef CONFIG_USER_NS
